{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"**No.** An Irish ICAV sub-fund does **not** have separate legal personality; the ICAV itself is the incorporated legal entity.\n\nHowever, [section 35 of the ICAV Act 2015](https://www.irishstatutebook.ie/eli/2015/act/2/section/35/enacted/en/html) provides **statutory segregated liability** between sub-funds. Liabilities incurred on behalf of, or attributable to, one sub-fund must be discharged solely from that sub-fund’s assets—not those of another sub-fund.\n\nThis is a statutory ring-fence within one legal entity, not a structure of separately incorporated subsidiaries. Recognition of that segregation outside Ireland can depend on the relevant foreign jurisdiction.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Legal personality determines *who the legal person is*; segregated liability determines *which assets can satisfy particular liabilities*. One does not require the other."}}
